This licence covers the MifBlender add-on - this folder - only. The free MCP
server published beside it has its own license, in its own folder.

Why the add-on is licensed this way: Blender's licence page treats add-ons that
use its Python API as needing a GPL-compatible licence when they are published,
and MIT is GPL-compatible.

The socket framing (framing.py) and the main-thread job marshalling (server.py)
are adapted from blender-mcp, https://github.com/MCPBlender/blender-mcp, whose
licence requires its notice to travel with the code:

